WEBVTT

00:08:58.912 --> 00:09:02.579
There's another emotional factor that
fuels these kinds of escalation traps

00:09:03.121 --> 00:09:09.037
anticipated regrette. You're worried
you'll wish you hadn't pulled the plug in.

00:09:09.037 --> 00:09:13.412
The NBA managers were afraid of giving
up too soon on a potential star.

00:09:13.579 --> 00:09:17.246
They're thinking about maybe trading a
particular athlete to another team,

00:09:17.246 --> 00:09:20.579
but then they're thinking, oh my God,
he's not done very well with us.

00:09:20.579 --> 00:09:21.871
But what if he suddenly blooms?

00:09:21.871 --> 00:09:25.246
But I'm watching him on the other team,
then I'm going to feel even worse.

00:09:26.246 --> 00:09:28.954
You probably know that voice
inside your head,

00:09:29.329 --> 00:09:31.662
what are you doing? You
can't give up too soon.